id: SCA-057
title: Committed .env file with secret values
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  filenames: .env .env.local .env.production
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: (DATABASE_URL|DB_PASSWORD|AWS_SECRET|API_KEY|PRIVATE_KEY|SECRET_KEY|AUTH_TOKEN)\s*=\s*[^\$\{]\S+
    message: Committed .env file exposes secrets (database passwords, API keys, cloud credentials). Automated scrapers continuously scan public repos for these.
fix: Add .env* to .gitignore. Use .env.example with placeholder values. Use a secrets manager in production.
